  "schema": "arcpuzzles-parametric-prototype-evidence-v1",
  "scope": "# Review \u2014 `05409de4bec8`\nTask/source: production generator `5.0.0`, SHA-256 `eb5433a5ff10d59419a771cf02ca4378fcbaffdb2835599c86fe160c6fb37fc9`; canonical `RULE_HASH = dfbf6efa8173`; both are unchanged.\nDefect: the retained unapproved prototype exported each public challenge while iterating private settings, so filesystem creation order exposed hidden setting order and a late filename collision could leave a partial public batch.\nRepair: derive exact visible bytes and full SHA-256 IDs with `reviewer_support`, validate and plan the whole batch first, reject duplicate visible payloads, preflight every destination, then write only in public-ID order; the setting-to-path map remains private.\nFocused checks: `18 passed` in `tests/test_parametric_rectangle_policy.py`, including hidden-order invariance, private-data invariance, visible-data sensitivity, duplicate rejection, exact-byte writes, and no-partial-write collision handling.\nRacket evidence: two fixed-per-episode settings, each with five demonstrations and four distinct queries; every label and rival output executed through Racket, and all four queries reject the other setting.\nIndependent check: exact public-byte hashes, full IDs, visible-only shape, private/public projection parity, unique 5+4 inputs, current verifier binding, and complete manifest all pass.\nReference-rule changes: none. Production generator behavior and canonical Racket authority are unchanged.\nStatus: the `rectangle_policy = longer | both` extension remains **proposed and unapproved**; packaging does not imply catalog approval or training admission.\nScope limit: no production battery was run because production behavior did not change; evidence is finite for two retained seeds and one declared rival.\n\n## Concrete changes",
  "task_id": "05409de4bec8",
